# Defense against the npm cross-arch lockfile pruning bug.
#
# When `npm install` (npm ≤ 11.2, including the npm 10.x bundled with
# Node 22) runs on one OS/CPU, it silently strips platform-specific
# `optionalDependencies` for *other* platforms from package-lock.json.
# The next `npm ci` on a different architecture then can't find the
# native binding and the build fails — the rolldown
# "Cannot find native binding" error path that hit this repo in
# commits 3ee82ed / b41a148.
#
# Fixed in npm >= 11.3 (PR npm/cli#8184). CI is pinned to npm >= 11.11.1
# (see .github/workflows/deploy-gh-pages.yml) so this is belt-and-braces:
# `include=optional` guarantees optional deps are resolved into the
# lockfile tree even if a future parent .npmrc / env / CI runner image
# leaks `omit=optional`.
#
# References:
#   - https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/7961  (root cause — pruning)
#   - https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/8184  (the fix PR)
#   - https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/4828  (the original report)
#   - https://github.com/rolldown/rolldown/issues/9068 (project hit)
include=optional